<title>USA: Alliance Bancorp to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Alliance Bancorp to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>HINSDALE, Ill. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliance Bancorp, the holding company for Liberty Federal Bank, said Friday it plans to repurchase up to 10 percent of its 5,333,844 shares of outstanding common stock, as authorized by the board of directors.  </p>
<p>The repurchases will be made from time to time in open market transactions or through privately negotiated transactions, the company said.</p>
<p>Alliance Bancorp is the parent company of Liberty Federal Bank, which was recently formed through the merger of Hinsdale Federal Bank of Hinsdale, Ill., and Liberty Federal Savings Bank of Chicago.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
